<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Petrocorii</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Vesunna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the Dordogne whose name lives on in the Périgord and whose town Vesunna became Périgueux.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Petrocorii lived in the valleys of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isle-river">Isle</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dordogne">Dordogne</a>, in the modern Dordogne. Their name is usually read as the four armies, perhaps a league of four communities. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> notes their iron workings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their rulers. Their main oppidum stood at La Curade near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perigueux">Périgueux</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They sent five thousand men to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alesia">Alesia</a> in 52 BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perigueux">Vesunna</a>, a well-preserved town whose temple tower, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tour-de-vesone">Tour de Vésone</a>, still stands. The city became Périgueux, and the medieval <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-perigord">County of Périgord</a> kept their name.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/petrocorii.jpg" alt="Petrocorii" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Pétrocores (peuple celtique de Gaule). Autorité émettrice de monnaie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Stat%C3%A8re,_or,_fonds_celtique,_P%C3%A9trocores_-_btv1b112863095_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vesunna</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=petrocorii" aria-label="Petrocorii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4697 583 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Petrocorii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5017 839L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5017 839h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5017 839h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vesunna. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=petrocorii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

